        "intervals_equal_1(..., true) compares property values with Fequal. Emaxx now uses ordinary equality for those values, preserving their contents while ignoring nested string properties. Existing interval-boundary and property-order comparison remains.",
        "String hashing reads actual storage bytes directly, removing the decoded text and extended-character allocations. Property-value hashing uses ordinary equality, as hash_interval does.",
        "The dumper writes key/value entries rather than cached hashes; load.rs reconstructs every standard hash after relocation. The existing dump/thaw contract now also checks unibyte, byte8 and private-use keys without removing an old assertion.",
        "The exact four ordinary GNU fixture inputs and expected output bytes are retained. Together they cover storage distinctions, symbol names and position policy, bad arguments, nested properties, mutation, collection, differing interval segmentation and custom hash-table lookup/replacement/removal."
